// expect-error: pin(call_arena) cannot hold: this value is not served by that arena
// expect-error: and a bracketed callee may have exactly one
//
// SPEC 5.4.1 for a *placement* pin, on the exact regression SPEC 5.2.1.1 admits
// it is silent about.
//
// Regime (a) brackets a call only while its callee has exactly one call site in
// the program. `make` has two, both inside `call_arena`, so the bracket is
// dropped and every allocation in `make` goes back to the heap. **Nothing else
// about this program changes**: it still compiles, still returns the same value,
// still passes every other test in this suite, and runs slower. That is the
// failure mode SPEC 5.2.1.1 asks the manifest to record, and the reason a record
// is not enough -- somebody has to read the diff.
//
// `pin(call_arena)` is that fact asserted, so the build stops here instead.
//
// **Delete the second call and this program compiles**, which is what makes this
// fixture discriminate rather than merely fail. The test runner performs the
// inverse edit on `test_63_placement_pin.psm` -- a program known to compile --
// and requires the mutant to be rejected, so neither direction rests on a reader
// believing this comment.
//
// The error is at the `let`, one function away from the edit that caused it, and
// the note is what closes that distance: it names `make`, its call-site count and
// the obligation. A diagnostic that only said "not served" would send a reader
// looking for a missing `region` in a function that never had one.

struct Cmd {
    id: Int,
    weight: Int
}

fn make(i: Int) -> Cmd {
    let pin(call_arena) c = Cmd { id: i, weight: i * 2 }
    return c
}

fn main() -> Int {
    let mut total = 0
    region call_arena {
        let mut i = 0
        while (i < 4) {
            let keep = make(i)
            total = total + keep.id
            i = i + 1
        }
        // The whole of the regression. One more call, inside the same region, so
        // obligation 3 still holds for both sites and nothing but the call count
        // separates this from `test_63_placement_pin.psm`.
        let extra = make(99)
        total = total + extra.id
    }
    return total - total
}
